op the russians reorganizing their  troops what the russians want to do is  to draw a line from kharkiv down to  mario paul to to push southwards to push  northwards and insulate isolate the  ukrainian troops who are the wrong side  of that line and so what what forces  does the ukrainians have in this area  will they be able to easily repel the  russians there what are the choices  there for them well they've got 10  brigades which is about 50 000 troops  and they are the best of the ukrainian  army so it's about a third of the  ukrainian army is in that area um and if  they are encircled they either have to  choose to fight the encirclement or  maybe withdraw give up the the fight as  it were in the east in order to live  another day and perhaps defend kiev in  the weeks to come and so even if the  russians are successful in taking this  region which again is just zoomed in on  only the southeast of the nation i guess  it's all relative because even odessa in  this region is a long way from the red  shaded area so it's it's a kind of  reduced objective of the russians for  sure  the russians were clearly pushing  westwards to odessa that was a big  strategic objective in order to landlock  ukraine to actually cut off all of their  access to the sea  they are further away from odessa now  than they were because mikolayev has  held and they've been pushed back east  from nikolayev so that looks as if it's  a big strategic objective which has gone  in obeyance while the russians think  about a much more as a big but minor  objective of trying to encircle  ukrainian forces in the east defence and  security analyst michael clark as always  thanks so much uh that's the latest for  now
 

